1|0@relationships^1440210217#cubeleq:damaskrose$:I don't think there's anything wrong with accepting help when it's offered (assuming they can afford it). But at the same time, you can't expect it's going to last forever, and you should probably have a backup plan. Even if they *wanted* to let you live there forever, sometimes people make poor financial decisions or simply have bad luck. And if that happened, they might end up *needing* to collect rental income, or even sell the house. So my opinion is that if someone offers you help, you can go ahead and take it - but don't take it for granted. Also, how can you be sure your parents are going to side with you over your sister? Sounds like she had dibs on the place before you did. 
